      "sequence_position": 2,
      "problem": "Using the cumulative distribution function table of the Poisson random variable $X∼\\text{Po}(14)$ given below, find the value of $P(X\\le 10).$\n\n| $\\,x\\,$ | $5$ | $6$ | $7$ | $8$ | $9$ | $10$ | $11$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $P(X\\le x)$ | $\\,0.0055\\,$ | $\\,0.0142\\,$ | $\\,0.0316\\,$ | $\\,0.0621\\,$ | $\\,0.1094\\,$ | $\\,0.1757\\,$ | $\\,0.2600\\,$ |",
      "worked_solution": "The cumulative distribution function of a discrete random variable $X$ is a function $F(x)$ such that\n\n$$\nF(x)=P(X\\le x).\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X\\le 10) & =F(10) \\\\  & =0.1757.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
